[7m# Q1: Migrating ~40 Ingresses from ingress-nginx to Gateway API[27m

[7m**Approach:** run both side by side and move traffic slowly. ingress-nginx stays up as the fallback until the end.[27m

[7m**Order:**[27m
[7m1. List all 40 Ingresses and note what each one uses: annotations, rewrites, auth, timeouts, TLS, snippets. Pick a Gateway API implementation and check it covers those.[27m
[7m2. Install the Gateway API CRDs and the new controller next to ingress-nginx, with its own load balancer address.[27m
[7m3. Convert the least important Ingress first, and test it by calling the new address directly, without changing DNS.[27m
[7m4. Convert the rest in small batches. Compare the r